.TH sane\-epsonv39 5 "31 Oct 2026" "@PACKAGEVERSION@" "SANE Scanner Access Now Easy"
.IX sane\-epsonv39
.SH NAME
sane\-epsonv39 \- SANE backend for the Epson Perfection V39 (GT\-S650) USB flatbed scanner
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B sane\-epsonv39
library implements a SANE (Scanner Access Now Easy) backend for the
Epson Perfection V39, sold as GT\-S650 in Japan (USB ID 04b8:013d).
.PP
This scanner is "host-based": it has no firmware in flash and does not
understand Epson's ESC/I command language. The backend uploads the
firmware after every power-on, calibrates the sensor before each scan, and
assembles the image on the host. It was written from an independent
description of the USB protocol and contains no Epson code.
.SH HARDWARE SUPPORT
.TP
.B Perfection V39 / GT\-S650 (04b8:013d)
Colour, gray and line-art at 75 to 4800 dpi over the full 8.5" x 11.7"
(216 x 297 mm) area. The hardware scans at 300, 600, 1200, 2400 and
4800 dpi; 75 to 200 dpi are produced by averaging a 300 dpi scan. Gray at
4800 dpi is averaged from a colour scan. The four front-panel buttons are
reported as sensor options.
.TP
.B Perfection V19 (04b8:013c)
Untested. Epson's Windows package for the V19 contains the same firmware
and scan code as the V39 one. Enable it with a
.B usb
line in the configuration file and please report the result.
.SH FIRMWARE
The backend needs Epson's firmware file
.IR esfw010c.bin ,
which may not be distributed with SANE. It is contained in Epson's Windows
driver package for the Perfection V39
.RI ( V39_EScan_3950_AM.exe ,
inside
.IR ModUsd.cab ),
which can be unpacked with
.BR 7z (1).
The backend looks for the file in this order:
.IP 1. 4
the path in the environment variable
.BR SANE_EPSONV39_FIRMWARE ;
.IP 2. 4
the
.B firmware
line of the configuration file;
.IP 3. 4
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/sane/epsonv39/
or
.IR ~/.local/share/sane/epsonv39/ ;
.IP 4. 4
.IR @DATADIR@/sane/epsonv39/ ,
.IR /usr/share/sane/epsonv39/ ,
.I /usr/share/iscan/
(Epson's own Linux plugin) and
.IR /usr/lib/firmware/epson/ .
.PP
After a power-on, the first scan takes about ten seconds longer while the
firmware starts and the scanner initialises.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-mode Color|Gray|Lineart
Selects the scan mode. Line-art is a threshold of the gray scan.
.TP
.B \-\-resolution 75|100|150|200|300|600|1200|2400|4800
Selects the resolution in dpi.
.TP
.B \-\-threshold 0..255
Black/white threshold in line-art mode (default 128).
.TP
.B \-\-preview[=(yes|no)]
Scans at 75 dpi.
.TP
.B \-l \-t \-x \-y
Top-left corner, width and height of the scan area in mm.
.TP
.B \-\-calibration\-cache[=(yes|no)]
The analog front-end offsets and LED exposure found by a scan are kept in
scanner RAM until power-off. A later scan in the same mode and resolution
checks them with one read each instead of searching again, which saves
1 to 3 seconds. The dark and white shading passes run on every scan. Set
to
.B no
to force a full calibration (default yes).
.TP
.B \-\-scan \-\-copy \-\-email \-\-pdf
Read-only sensors for the Start, Copy, Scan to E\-mail and PDF buttons.
They are true only while the button is held down, so tools such as
.BR scanbd (8)
must poll them several times a second. They read as released during a
scan.
.SH CONFIGURATION FILE
The configuration file
.I @CONFIGDIR@/epsonv39.conf
supports these lines; empty lines and lines starting with a hash mark (#)
are ignored:
.TP
.BI firmware " path"
Location of
.IR esfw010c.bin .
.TP
.BI usb " vendor product"
A USB device to use, for example
.BR "usb 0x04b8 0x013c" .
Without any
.B usb
line, the backend uses 04b8:013d only.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I @CONFIGDIR@/epsonv39.conf
The backend configuration file.
.TP
.I @LIBDIR@/libsane\-epsonv39.a
The static library implementing this backend.
.TP
.I @LIBDIR@/libsane\-epsonv39.so
The shared library implementing this backend (present on systems that
support dynamic loading).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SANE_CONFIG_DIR
This environment variable specifies the list of directories that may
contain the configuration file. See
.BR sane\-dll (5).
.TP
.B SANE_EPSONV39_FIRMWARE
Path of the firmware file; overrides all other locations.
.TP
.B SANE_DEBUG_EPSONV39
Debug level: 1 shows errors and scan summaries, 2 adds calibration
results and timings, 3 every AFE and LED measurement and the reader's
result, 4 every image transfer and button reading. USB traffic is logged
with
.BR SANE_DEBUG_SANEI_USB .
.SH KNOWN ISSUES
If the scanner stops answering (time-outs), unplug it or switch it off and
on; the backend uploads the firmware again. A USB reset in software can
leave it unable to reconnect until it is replugged.
.PP
Only one calibration-cache entry exists, so alternating between modes
recalibrates every time.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sane (7),
.BR sane\-usb (5),
.BR scanimage (1),
.BR scanbd (8)
.PP
The protocol description and reference captures:
.I https://github.com/makkara/epson-v39
.SH AUTHOR
makkara
